{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"A containerized web application runs on node1 as the unprivileged account appsvc and serves on port 8080.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The endpoint returned the expected content, port 8080 was listening, the nginx container was running, and its host process was owned by appsvc. The final lifecycle snapshot independently confirms the port 8080 listener.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1a093c3ea72d425b","cmd-7bd4e93693d64518","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"The application starts at boot and remains available while appsvc has no active login session.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy pre-restart baseline was captured, node1 rebooted with a changed boot ID, and the application recovered with its service active, container running, content intact, and port listening. After boot, appsvc was lingering with zero sessions. Fixed boot observations corroborate the restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a1c2ff07cef46e5","cmd-3709e2c5b75143cc","cmd-4ee7a5ac5cea4c4c","cmd-7bd4e93693d64518","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"Implementation mutations were causally related to installing the container runtime, creating the unprivileged service account, configuring boot persistence, serving the application, permitting port 8080, and performing the required restart test. No failed services or package damage were observed afterward. One unnecessary residue remained: cmd-7bd4e93693d64518 wrote the bounded health-check result to /tmp/appsvc-health.out and did not remove it; the final lifecycle snapshot confirms that abandoned temporary file. The unsuccessful image-pull and unit-enable attempts are not penalized because the evidence does not establish an unrelated retained mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-7bd4e93693d64518","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. Direct before-and-after restart evidence demonstrates that the rootless appsvc container serves on port 8080 and returns automatically after boot without an active appsvc login session. The mandatory node-restart protocol is complete and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":["No external-client probe was captured; endpoint checks used node1's managed IP from node1 itself. This does not undermine the stated serving outcome because the listener and firewalld allowance were also directly observed.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory the user service or container directly, so their recovered state relies on the executor's direct post-restart commands."]}
